# WHAT SURVIVES A RELAUNCH (docs/tasks-s4-plan.md P7, §4). Act one writes
# a task, a setting, an appearance and a window frame; `relaunch launch`
# is the PLAIN door — the runner starts the same artifact the way a user
# would, with nothing pending — and act two reads all four back, each
# through the mechanism that owns it: the task out of the app's own SQLite
# document under app_data_dir(), the setting and the appearance out of the
# preferences store, the frame out of kaya's own window memory.
#
# ONE `relaunch` PER SCENE is the rule (docs/tasks-s9-plan.md R6a), so the
# notification door's second act stays in tasks.steps and the plain door
# gets this file. The guest is the same task manager (rusthost maps the
# scene name to tasks::app), and the ids are tasks.steps'.
#
# The clock is fixed at Monday 2026-09-07 under the harness, so the seed
# routes exactly as it does there: two tasks in Inbox.
expect_title "tasks"
expect_section "Inbox"
expect label@inbox_count "2 in inbox"

# THE DATA. A quick-added task is the app's own document's to keep: it
# lands in Inbox as t10, the first key past the nine the seed minted.
set_text entry@quick "Water the plants"
click button@add
expect label@inbox_count "3 in inbox"
expect label@title[t10] "Water the plants"
expect entry@quick ""

# THE SETTINGS, through the Settings screen the View menu pushes. Week
# starts Sunday is `week_start` = 1 in the preferences store; the
# appearance choice is the app's, applied process-wide (S2b) and read back
# from the PLATFORM, never from the prop.
menu_activate "View>Settings"
expect_entries 1
expect label@settings[s] "Week starts Monday; badge shown; completed move to Logbook"
choose select@week[s] 1
expect label@settings[s] "Week starts Sunday; badge shown; completed move to Logbook"
choose select@appearance[s] 2
expect_appearance "dark"
back
expect_entries 0

# THE FRAME. Desktops only — the phones have no window frame and their
# legs drop this line and its assertion in act two.
resize_window 900x620

relaunch launch

# ACT TWO runs in the process the runner started, which has none of act
# one's memory: no scene in its environment, no model, no window.
expect_title "tasks"
expect_section "Inbox"
expect label@inbox_count "3 in inbox"
expect label@title[t10] "Water the plants"
expect_appearance "dark"
menu_activate "View>Settings"
expect_entries 1
expect label@settings[s] "Week starts Sunday; badge shown; completed move to Logbook"
back
expect_entries 0
# THE PLATFORM'S OWN STORE, re-read (§4): the suite re-opened on Apple,
# the preferences file re-read elsewhere — never kaya's memory of its own
# write. A setting nobody changed was never written, which is what the
# absent one says.
expect_pref week_start "1"
expect_no_pref hide_badge
expect_window_size 900x620
